    "historical_hypothesis_verbatim": "[HYPOTHESIS] Prediction written before measuring (from the EXP-009 pilot): on Qwen3-30B-A3B, below one token's expert footprint (~1.02 GiB, 384 experts) the runtime's sharded LRU collapses (pilot replay: 0-20% expert hits at 1 GiB, ~0-2% at 768 MiB), while frequency-based retention would keep ~30-45%. If the runtime keeps more than 30% expert-level hits at 768 MiB, the prediction is falsified.",
    "h5": {
      "model": "30b",
      "budget": "768M",
      "budget_bytes": 805306368,
      "phase": "diag",
      "threshold": 0.3,
      "comparison": "strictly greater than",
      "metric_field": "manifest.final_store_stats.expert_level_hit_rate",
      "metric_definition": "EXP-020 workload gate-slice hit rate: slice hits over slice accesses made in the gate (first) MUL_MAT_ID node of each layer, prefill + decode, workload requests only (warm-up and flush sentinel excluded); computed by argine.research.rawlog.node_attributed_outcomes from the research trace of the launch. It is the runtime field `expert_level_hit_rate`, not the expert-event decode-only counterfactual metric of the EXP-009 pilot.",
      "aggregation": "arithmetic mean over the H-5-eligible launches of the 30B diag block at 768 MiB (2 scheduled); individual launches and dispersion reported; no launch-level vote",
      "eligibility": "launch outcome VALID, manifest publication_quality true, trace complete over the workload, budget_violations == 0",
      "minimum_eligible_launches": 1,
      "falsified_if": "aggregate > 0.30",
      "otherwise": "not falsified by this test; formal status INCONCLUSIVE",
      "not_evaluable": "0 eligible launches (or the 30B diag block incomplete): formal status INCONCLUSIVE, reported as not evaluable, with the outcomes observed at 768 MiB",
      "positive_support_threshold": null,
      "positive_support_note": "No positive support threshold is introduced. The 2026-10-03 prediction recorded only a falsification condition; any support bound chosen now (e.g. <=10%, <=2%, a fraction of the 1.5G anchor) would be selected after the pilot values were known. Agreement with the predicted range may be reported descriptively only."
